# IGDB data dumps first

Partner dumps: [IGDB Data Dumps](https://api-docs.igdb.com/#data-dumps) (`GET /v4/dumps`, then `/v4/dumps/{endpoint}`).

Local sync lives in [`igdb_dumps.py`](igdb_dumps.py) → DB tables `igdb_*`, refreshed ~daily only while a product feature needs those endpoints (`needed_endpoints`).

## When designing or extending a feature

1. **Check the dump catalog** — does the needed entity exist as a dump endpoint (games, companies, genres, game_modes, covers, artworks, external_games, involved_companies, …)?
2. **Prefer local dumps** — propose storing/querying via `igdb_dumps` + DB instead of new live Apicalypse calls to `api.igdb.com`.
3. **Reuse existing tables** when possible; if a new endpoint is required, add it to `_ENDPOINT_TABLE` / feature packs in `igdb_dumps.py` and gate sync with `needed_endpoints`.
4. **Live IGDB API** only when dumps clearly cannot cover the need (write path, real-time-only field, etc.) — say so explicitly.
5. **Attribution** — user-facing IGDB data still needs credit to [IGDB.com](https://www.igdb.com) (Help /feedback, feature prompts, README/guide as appropriate). See [`api-license-compliance.mdc`](api-license-compliance.mdc).

## Already on dumps

| Surface | Local endpoints |
|---|---|
| «Мне повезёт» / lucky | games, external_games (+ covers/artworks pack with users) |
| Ignore genres/publishers | companies, genres, game_modes, involved, games, external |
| Alert game cover image | covers → artworks via Twitch uid map |
| `{game_description}` in alerts | games (`summary`) + external_games via Twitch uid |

Twitch Helix (category search, live streams by `game_id`) is separate — not replaced by IGDB dumps.
